## Upper body (blouse / kameez / kurti)
| Tailor measurement | How it is taken | Src | Flat-garment equivalent |
|---|---|---|---|
| Bust | Fullest part of bust and widest part of back, tape horizontal all round | 1,2,3,4,5 | pit-to-pit x 2 |
| Waist / "around above waist" | Natural waist; blouse: just above the waist; kameez: one finger above navel, firm not tight; or string settled at natural waist | 1,2,4,5 | waist width x 2 |
| Hip | Fullest part of hips, an index finger fits between tape and body | 2,5 | hip width x 2 |
| Shoulder width | One shoulder tip to the other, across the back | 1,3,5 | seam-to-seam |
| Sleeve length | Edge of shoulder down the arm to the chosen end | 1,2,3,4 | shoulder seam to cuff |
| Around arm | Fullest part of the bicep | 1,2 | not in spec yet |
| Kameez/blouse length | From the **centre of the shoulder** straight down, tape passes over centre of bust | 1,2 | neck-shoulder point to hem (see note A) |
| Front neck depth | Top of shoulder at neck joint down to where the neck ends | 1,2 | not in spec yet |
| Back neck depth | Neck joint to centre of back, as deep as wanted | 1,2 | not in spec yet |
| Armhole round | Listed for Punjabi-style kameez | 2 | not in spec yet |
| Back length | Nape of neck to hem | 5 | needs back view |

## Lower body (for trouser / salwar / churidar specs, not built yet)
| Tailor measurement | How it is taken | Src |
|---|---|---|
| Waist | Around the stomach just above the upper hip bone | 2 |
| Thigh | Fullest part of the thigh | 2 |
