## Notes and open items
- **A. Length convention mismatch.** Tailors measure length from the centre of the shoulder. The spec uses the neck-shoulder (high point) point, which is what is visible on a flat garment. Ask the leader which convention the company's size charts use; the difference is a few cm and changes accuracy numbers.
- **B. Ease.** Garment size minus body size. Source 2 only hints at it ("allow an index finger" for hip). No numbers found; values must come from a tailor or the leader. Left `null` in specs.
- **C.** Hip level: sources say "fullest part"; no distance from the waist is given. Spec uses "widest point of the garment below the waist".
- **D.** Sleeve length from a flat photo is a straight-line approximation of the along-the-arm measure.
- **E.** Not capturable from one flat top-down photo: neck depths, armhole round, bicep, back length. Would need extra views or a different method.
- Do not cite unknown mirror sites that host copies of a "Saree Blouse Measurement Chart" PDF.